Native libm.h delta: avoid `long double` for 6c
================================================

Native Plan 9 6c has no `long double` type.  generated9's musl libm.h
declares unused long-double helpers unconditionally:

    static inline long double fp_barrierl(long double x) { ... }
    static inline void fp_force_evall(long double x) { ... }
    hidden int __rem_pio2l(long double, long double *);
    hidden long double __sinl(long double, long double, int);
    ...

None of the 49 math/*.c files in the vendored set implements or calls those
long-double entry points; they are present only because musl's shared
libm.h covers the full libm.  vendor.rc rewrites `long double` to `double`
in math/libm.h so 6c can parse the header:

    sed 's/long double/double/g' math/libm.h > math/libm.h.new
    mv math/libm.h.new math/libm.h

This is a source-level adaptation, not a change to the double-precision
algorithms.  If a future math file needs true x87 80-bit long double, this
shortcut must be revisited and 6c support investigated.
